==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|pech}}, {{m|gmh|bech}}, from {{inh|de|goh|peh}}, {{m|goh|beh}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*pik}}, from {{der|de|la|pix}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|pek}}, {{cog|en|pitch}}.

The form is unusual as it shows unshifted ''p-'', but shifted ''-ch'', even though the shift of initial ''p-'' to ''pf-'' occurred later than that of postvocalic ''-k'' to ''-ch''. [[w:de:Theodor Frings|Theodor Frings]] therefore considered that the word was at first restricted to [[West Central German]] along the Rhine (which lacks the ''pf''-shift) and only spread to [[Upper German]] slightly later when the shift was no longer active. ({{m+|gmh||pfich}} occurs only once in a Central German text from the 14th century and is thus probably a hypercorrection.)

